# ---------------- 5 Dataflow and streaming machines (slides 16-20)
add("5","abts2020tsp","Abts, Ross, Sparling et al. (Groq)",2020,"Think fast: a tensor streaming processor (TSP) for accelerating deep learning workloads (ISCA 2020)",None,"https://groq.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/02/2020-Isca.pdf","Primary paper. One core of functional slices on a 25 x 29 mm 14 nm die, 26.8 billion transistors, 220 MiB of SRAM at about 55 TiB/s, 820 TOPS at 1 GHz (900 MHz nominal), no caches or arbiters; ResNet-50 at 20.4K images/s at batch 1. Slides 5, 6 and 16.")
add("5","abts2022tsm","Abts, Kimmell, Ling, Kim et al. (Groq)",2022,"A software-defined tensor streaming multiprocessor for large-scale machine learning (ISCA 2022)",None,"https://groq.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/02/GroqISCAPaper2022_ASoftwareDefinedTensorStreamingMultiprocessorForLargeScaleMachineLearning.pdf","Primary paper. Determinism extended to the network: 8-TSP nodes, 72-TSP racks, a Dragonfly to 10,440 TSPs, 722 ns per hop, forward error correction and software replay instead of link retry. Slides 16 and 31.")
add("5","groq2024aa","Groq",2024,"Groq LPU inference engine leads in first independent LLM benchmark (February 13, 2024)",None,"https://groq.com/newsroom/groq-lpu-inference-engine-leads-in-first-independent-llm-benchmark","Vendor press release. Llama 2 Chat 70B at 241 tokens/s on Artificial Analysis, the first independent LLM API measurement of a non-GPU chip. Slides 16 and 33.")
add("5","dcd2025nvidiagroq","DatacenterDynamics",2025,"Nvidia to license tech from AI inference chip company Groq, hire its leadership (December 2025)",None,"https://www.datacenterdynamics.com/en/news/nvidia-to-license-tech-from-ai-inference-chip-company-groq-hire-its-leadership/","Press, secondary source. A non-exclusive license plus the hiring of Jonathan Ross and Sunny Madra; the $20B figure reported by CNBC and not confirmed; Groq stays independent with GroqCloud. Slides 16, 34 and 35.")
add("5","register2026lpx","Mann (The Register)",2026,"Nvidia slaps $20B Groq tech into massive new LPX racks to speed AI response time (March 16, 2026)",None,"https://www.theregister.com/2026/03/16/nvidia_lpx_groq_3/","Press, secondary source. The GTC 2026 LPX rack: 256 LPUs, about 500 MB of SRAM and 150 TB/s per LPU, 1.2 PF FP8 each, shipping later in 2026; in NVIDIA's split the LPX runs the FFN and MoE half of decode and speculative drafts, while Vera Rubin does prefill, attention and the KV cache. Slides 16 and 31.")
add("5","tomshw2026lpx","Tom's Hardware",2026,"Nvidia presents Groq 3 LPX architecture and unveils its first third-party inference benchmark (August 26, 2026)",None,"https://tomshardware.com/tech-industry/semiconductors/nvidia-presents-groq-3-lpx-architecture-and-unveils-its-first-third-party-inference-benchmark","Press, secondary source. Hot Chips 2026: LP30 with no HBM, 350 ns chip to chip; 256 chips give 128 GB, 40 PB/s and 315 PF FP8; Gemma 4 31B at 3,431 tokens/s on a private endpoint at concurrency 1; in production. Slides 16 and 33.")
add("5","prabhakar2024sn40l","Prabhakar, Sivaramakrishnan, Gandhi, Du, ... Olukotun (SambaNova)",2024,"SambaNova SN40L: scaling the AI memory wall with dataflow and composition of experts (MICRO 2024)","2405.07518",None,"Primary paper. The three-tier SRAM, HBM and DDR design; Samba-CoE with 150 experts and about a trillion parameters on one 8-socket node, 15 to 31 times faster model switching, 3.7 times a DGX H100. Slides 8 and 17.")
add("5","prabhakar2024hotchips","Prabhakar (SambaNova)",2024,"SambaNova SN40L RDU: breaking the barrier of trillion+ parameter scale gen AI computing (Hot Chips 2024 slides)",None,"https://www.hc2024.hotchips.org/assets/program/conference/day1/48_HC2024.Sambanova.Prabhakar.final-withoutvideo.pdf","Primary conference slides. TSMC 5 nm, 102 billion transistors, 1,040 PCUs and PMUs, 520 MB SRAM, 64 GB HBM at 1.6 TB/s, 1.5 TB DDR, 638 TFLOP/s BF16; 16 chips serve Llama 3.1 405B at 114 tokens/s. Slides 17 and 31.")
add("5","sambanova2026sn50","SambaNova Systems",2026,"SambaNova unveils fastest chip for agentic AI, collaborates with Intel, and raises $350M+ (February 24, 2026)",None,"https://www.businesswire.com/news/home/20260224971025/en/","Vendor press release. SN50: five times the SN40L's compute and four times its network, 256-chip domains, Llama 3.3 70B FP8 at 895 tokens/s per user against 184 on a B200 (vendor test); Series E and the Intel collaboration. Slides 17 and 34.")
add("5","jia2019ipu","Jia, Tillman, Maggioni and Scarpazza (Citadel)",2019,"Dissecting the Graphcore IPU architecture via microbenchmarking","1912.03413",None,"Independent measurement paper. GC2: 1,216 tiles, 304 MiB of SRAM, 30.7 TB/s measured against 45 nominal, 133 ns exchange latency, 64 GB/s IPU-Links; the only outside look at the IPU. Slides 18 and 31.")
add("5","wardfoxton2022bow","Ward-Foxton (EE Times Asia)",2022,"Graphcore supercharges IPU with wafer-on-wafer (March 9, 2022)",None,"https://www.eetasia.com/?p=36263","Press, secondary source. Bow: a power-delivery wafer with deep-trench capacitors hybrid-bonded under the unchanged 7 nm IPU, 1.325 to 1.85 GHz, 350 TFLOP/s; Bow Pod systems from Pod16 to Pod1024; the planned 10-exaflop Good computer. (The $149,995 list price on slide 18 was the GC200 IPU-POD16 of June 2021, before Bow.) Slide 18.")
add("5","register2023graphcore","Robinson (The Register)",2023,"AI chip biz Graphcore seeks capital to remain going concern (October 6, 2023)",None,"https://www.theregister.com/2023/10/06/brit_ai_chip_outfit_graphcore/","Press, secondary source. The 2022 accounts: revenue $2.7M (down 46 percent), pre-tax loss $204.6M, staff from 631 to 494, a material going-concern uncertainty; the year before the SoftBank sale. Slides 18 and 35.")
add("5","register2024blackhole","The Register",2024,"Tenstorrent's Blackhole chips boast 768 RISC-V cores and almost as many FLOPS (August 27, 2024)",None,"https://www.theregister.com/2024/08/27/tenstorrent_ai_blackhole/","Press, secondary source. The Hot Chips 36 Blackhole talk: 140 Tensix, 16 big and 752 baby RISC-V cores, 745 TFLOP/s FP8 and 372 FP16, 10 x 400 GbE, 32-chip Galaxy at 23.8 PF FP8 with 1 TB. Slides 19 and 31.")
add("5","sth2025rebelquad","ServeTheHome",2025,"Rebellions REBEL-Quad UCIe and 144GB HBM3E accelerator at Hot Chips 2025 (August 24, 2025)",None,"https://www.servethehome.com/rebellions-rebel-quad-ucie-and-144gb-hbm3e-accelerator-at-hot-chips-2025/","Press, secondary source. Four Samsung SF4X chiplets on CoWoS-S joined by UCIe-A, four HBM3E sites (144 GB), Llama 3.3 70B at 35.5 ms per token on a development board. Slide 20.")
add("5","lam2024rngd","Lam (Chips and Cheese)",2024,"FuriosaAI's RNGD at Hot Chips 2024: accelerating AI with a more flexible primitive (September 11, 2024)",None,"https://chipsandcheese.com/p/furiosaais-rngd-at-hot-chips-2024-accelerating-ai-with-a-more-flexible-primitive","Independent analysis, secondary source. The written record of the RNGD talk: TSMC 5 nm, 1 GHz, 150 W, 48 GB HBM3 at 1.5 TB/s, 64 slices plus a spare per unit, 256 MB SRAM; the tensor-contraction primitive of Furiosa's ISCA 2024 paper. Slide 20.")

# ---------------- 6 Hyperscalers and established vendors (slides 21-24)
add("6","aws2023inferentia2","AWS Machine Learning Blog",2023,"AWS Inferentia2 builds on AWS Inferentia1 by delivering 4x higher throughput and 10x lower latency (June 13, 2023)",None,"https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/machine-learning/aws-inferentia2-builds-on-aws-inferentia1-by-delivering-4x-higher-throughput-and-10x-lower-latency/","Vendor blog. The Inferentia1 and 2 table: 128 against 380 TOPS INT8, 64 against 190 TFLOP/s BF16, 8 GB of DRAM at 50 GB/s against 32 GB of HBM at 820 GB/s, NeuronCore-v1 to v2. Slide 21.")
add("6","barr2024trn2","Barr (AWS)",2024,"Amazon EC2 Trn2 instances and Trn2 UltraServers for AI/ML training and inference are now available (December 3, 2024)",None,"https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/aws/amazon-ec2-trn2-instances-and-trn2-ultraservers-for-aiml-training-and-inference-is-now-available","Vendor blog. Trainium2: 8 NeuronCores, 96 GiB HBM at 2.9 TB/s, 1.3 PF FP8 dense (5.2 sparse); 16-chip instances on a 1 TB/s 2D torus; 64-chip UltraServers at 83 PF dense; 30 to 40 percent better price-performance than P5e (AWS claim). Slides 21 and 31.")
add("6","aws2025trn3","AWS",2025,"Amazon EC2 Trn3 UltraServers (product page)",None,"https://aws.amazon.com/ec2/instance-types/trn3/","Vendor page. Trainium3: AWS's first 3 nm chip, 144 GB HBM3e at 4.9 TB/s, 144-chip UltraServers at 362 PF MXFP8 with 20.7 TB and 706 TB/s, NeuronSwitch-v1 and NeuronLink-v4 (2.56 TB/s per chip in the Neuron documentation, the 2.6 TB/s on slide 21); 4.4 times Trn2 (AWS claim). Slide 21.")
add("6","techcrunch2025trn3","TechCrunch",2025,"Amazon releases an impressive new AI chip and teases an Nvidia-friendly roadmap (December 2, 2025)",None,"https://techcrunch.com/2025/12/02/amazon-releases-an-impressive-new-ai-chip-and-teases-a-nvidia-friendly-roadmap","Press, secondary source. Trainium3 at re:Invent 2025 and the Trainium4 preview with NVIDIA NVLink Fusion support, no date given. Slide 21.")
add("6","sth2024maia100","ServeTheHome",2024,"Microsoft Maia 100 AI accelerator for Azure (Hot Chips 2024)",None,"https://servethehome.com/microsoft-maia-100-ai-accelerator-for-azure","Press, secondary source. The Hot Chips 2024 talk: TSMC N5 on CoWoS-S, 64 GB HBM2E, about 500 MB of on-chip SRAM, 16 clusters of 4 tiles, 12 x 400 GbE, 700 W TDP (about 500 W in service), 6- and 9-bit formats. Slide 22.")
add("6","microsoft2026maia200","Microsoft Azure Infrastructure Blog",2026,"Deep dive into the Maia 200 architecture (January 2026)",None,"https://techcommunity.microsoft.com/blog/azureinfrastructureblog/deep-dive-into-the-maia-200-architecture/4489312","Vendor blog. Maia 200: TSMC N3P, 216 GB HBM3e at 7 TB/s, 272 MB SRAM, 10.15 PF FP4 and 5.07 PF FP8, 750 W, a 2.8 TB/s Ethernet scale-up link and 6,144-chip domains; deployed only inside Azure, with no BF16 figure published. Slides 22 and 31.")
add("6","meta2024mtiav2","Meta AI",2024,"Our next-generation Meta Training and Inference Accelerator (April 10, 2024)",None,"https://ai.meta.com/blog/next-generation-meta-training-inference-accelerator-AI-MTIA/","Vendor blog. The v1 against v2 table: 354 TOPS INT8 dense (708 sparse), 177 TFLOP/s BF16 dense, 256 MB SRAM at 2.7 TB/s, 128 GB LPDDR5 at 204.8 GB/s, 90 W, 1.35 GHz. Slides 22 and 31.")
add("6","hpcwire2026mtia","HPCwire",2026,"Meta packs gobs of HBM into homegrown AI accelerators (March 11, 2026)",None,"https://www.hpcwire.com/2026/03/11/meta-packs-gobs-of-hbm-into-homegrown-ai-accelerators/","Press, secondary source. The 2026 MTIA family: MTIA 400 at 1,200 W in 72-chip racks, MTIA 450 with 288 GB at 18.4 TB/s and 21 PF MX4, MTIA 500 with up to 512 GB, 27.6 TB/s, 30 PF MX4 and 1,700 W in 2027. Slide 22.")
add("6","tomshw2025openaibroadcom","Tom's Hardware",2025,"OpenAI, Broadcom to co-develop 10GW of custom AI chips (October 13, 2025)",None,"https://www.tomshardware.com/openai-broadcom-to-co-develop-10gw-of-custom-ai-chips","Press, secondary source. The deal terms: 10 GW of accelerators and racks, OpenAI designing and Broadcom building and deploying over Ethernet, from H2 2026 to the end of 2029. Slides 23 and 34.")
add("6","kaplan2024gaudi3","Kaplan (Intel)",2024,"Intel Gaudi 3 AI accelerator: architected for gen AI training and inference (Hot Chips 2024 slides)",None,"https://www.hc2024.hotchips.org/assets/program/conference/day1/60_HC2024.Intel.RomanKaplan.Gaudi3-0826.pdf","Primary conference slides. Two 5 nm dies, 8 MMEs and 64 TPCs, 96 MB SRAM at 12.8 TB/s, 128 GB HBM2e at 3.67 TB/s, 1,835 TFLOP/s for both BF16 and FP8 matrix, 900 W air or 1,200 W liquid, 24 x 200 GbE. Slide 24.")
add("6","qualcomm2023ultra","Qualcomm",2023,"Qualcomm Cloud AI 100 Ultra product brief",None,"https://www.qualcomm.com/content/dam/qcomm-martech/dm-assets/documents/Prod-Brief-QCOM-Cloud-AI-100-Ultra.pdf","Vendor datasheet. 64 AI cores, 870 TOPS INT8, 576 MB SRAM, 128 GB LPDDR4x at 548 GB/s, 150 W on a PCIe card. Slide 24.")
add("6","sth2025qualcommai200","Kennedy (ServeTheHome)",2025,"Qualcomm announces new integrated AI racks with 768GB cards and a 200MW AI deal (October 27, 2025)",None,"https://www.servethehome.com/qualcomm-announces-new-integrated-ai-racks-with-768gb-cards-and-a-200mw-ai-deal/","Press, secondary source. AI200 with 768 GB of LPDDR per card, AI250 with near-memory compute and a claimed 10 times effective bandwidth, about 160 kW liquid-cooled racks, Humain's 200 MW from 2026. Slides 24, 28 and 34.")
add("6","sth2024spyre","ServeTheHome",2024,"IBM Telum II processor and Spyre AI updates at Hot Chips 2024 (August 26, 2024)",None,"https://servethehome.com/ibm-telum-ii-processor-and-spyre-ai-updates-at-hot-chips-2024","Press, secondary source. Spyre: 32 cores with 2 MB scratchpads, Samsung 5 nm, 300 TOPS, 75 W, 128 GB LPDDR5 per card, eight cards per drawer as presented at Hot Chips (IBM's 2025 GA release gives up to 48 cards per z17 and 16 per Power11). Slide 24.")
add("6","talpes2022dojo","Talpes, Williams and Das Sarma (Tesla)",2022,"The microarchitecture of Tesla's exa-scale computer (Hot Chips 34 slides)",None,"https://hc34.hotchips.org/assets/program/conference/day2/Machine%20Learning/HotChips_tesla_dojo_uarch.pdf","Primary conference slides. D1: TSMC 7 nm, 645 mm2, 354 nodes at 2 GHz, 362 TFLOP/s BF16/CFP8, 440 MB SRAM, 2 TB/s per die edge; a 5 x 5 tile of known-good dies. Slide 24.")
add("6","techcrunch2025dojo","TechCrunch",2025,"Tesla Dojo: the rise and fall of Elon Musk's AI supercomputer (September 2, 2025)",None,"https://techcrunch.com/2025/09/02/tesla-dojo-the-rise-and-fall-of-elon-musks-ai-supercomputer/","Press, secondary source. Dojo shut down and its team disbanded in mid-August 2025, Dojo 2 called an evolutionary dead end, the $16.5B Samsung AI6 contract weeks earlier. Read with the January 2026 TechCrunch report of the Dojo3 restart. Slides 24 and 35.")
add("6","techcrunch2026dojo3","TechCrunch",2026,"Elon Musk says Tesla's restarted Dojo3 will be for space-based AI compute (January 20, 2026)",None,"https://techcrunch.com/2026/01/20/elon-musk-says-teslas-restarted-dojo3-will-be-for-space-based-ai-compute","Press, secondary source. Five months after the team was disbanded, Musk says Dojo3 is restarted on AI5-family silicon, aimed at space-based AI compute rather than Tesla's video training; why slide 24 says Tesla paused rather than stopped. Slides 3 and 24.")

# ---------------- 7 China (slides 25-27)
add("7","liao2019davinci","Liao, Tu, Xia and Zhou (Huawei)",2019,"DaVinci: a scalable architecture for neural network computing (Hot Chips 31 slides)",None,"https://www.old.hotchips.org/hc31/HC31_1.11_Huawei.Davinci.HengLiao_v4.0.pdf","Primary conference slides. The Da Vinci core's 16 x 16 x 16 cube (4,096 FP16 or 8,192 INT8 MACs per cycle) with vector and scalar units; Ascend 910 at 256 TFLOP/s FP16, 350 W, 7+ nm EUV. Slide 25.")
add("7","feldgoise2024cset","Feldgoise and Dohmen (CSET)",2024,"Pushing the limits: Huawei's AI chip tests U.S. export controls (June 17, 2024)",None,"https://cset.georgetown.edu/publication/pushing-the-limits-huaweis-ai-chip-tests-u-s-export-controls/","Analyst note, secondary source. Ascend 910 against 910B: TSMC 7 nm against SMIC N+2, 30-32 against 20-25 active cores, 320 against 400 TFLOP/s FP16 (part of the gain a counting change), HBM2e at up to 1.6 TB/s and 64 GB; low SMIC yields inferred. Slides 25 and 27.")
add("7","patel2025cm384","Patel, Nishball, Xie et al. (SemiAnalysis)",2025,"Huawei AI CloudMatrix 384: China's answer to Nvidia GB200 NVL72 (April 16, 2025)",None,"https://newsletter.semianalysis.com/p/huawei-ai-cloudmatrix-384-chinas-answer-to-nvidia-gb200-nvl72","Analyst note, secondary source. 384 Ascend 910C in 16 racks with 6,912 400G LPO transceivers, about 300 PF dense BF16, 3.6 times the HBM and 2.1 times the bandwidth of an NVL72 at about 3.9 times the power (about 559 kW against 145 kW, all-in; 2.3 times per FLOP, 1.8 per TB/s, 1.1 per TB); most 910B/C dies from TSMC via Sophgo, HBM mainly Samsung. Slides 25, 26 and 31.")
add("7","zuo2025cm384","Zuo, Lin, Deng et al. (Huawei Cloud)",2025,"Serving large language models on Huawei CloudMatrix384","2506.12708",None,"Primary paper. The system as Huawei describes it: 384 Ascend NPUs and 192 Kunpeng CPUs on the Unified Bus; DeepSeek-R1 served at 6,688 prefill and 1,943 decode tokens/s per NPU. Slide 26.")
add("7","huawei2025xukeynote","Xu (Huawei Connect 2025 keynote)",2025,"Groundbreaking SuperPoD interconnect: leading a new paradigm for AI infrastructure (September 18, 2025)",None,"https://www.huawei.com/en/news/2025/9/hc-xu-keynote-speech","Vendor keynote text. The Ascend 950PR (Q1 2026), 950DT (Q4 2026, HiZQ 2.0 HBM, 144 GB at 4 TB/s), 960 (Q4 2027) and 970 (Q4 2028); Atlas 950 (8,192 chips, 8 EF FP8) and 960 (15,488 chips, 30 EF FP8) SuperPoDs; UnifiedBus; the mainland 'will lag behind in process nodes'. The 960 and 970 dates and figures were revised in September 2026 (see the Tom's Hardware entry). Slides 25 and 26.")
add("7","tomshw2026ascendroadmap","Tom's Hardware",2026,"Huawei details AI accelerator roadmap, pulls in next-generation Ascend NPUs by quarters; FP4 performance of the Ascend 960PR doubles expectations (Huawei Connect 2026)",None,"https://www.tomshardware.com/tech-industry/artificial-intelligence/huawei-details-ai-accelerator-roadmap-pulls-in-next-generation-ascend-npus-by-quarters-fp4-performance-of-the-ascend-960pr-doubles-expectations","Press, secondary source. The September 18, 2026 revision: 960DT in Q1 2027 and 960PR in Q3 2027 (2 PF FP8, 8 PF FP4) with a 2.2 TB/s link; 970 in 2028 at 3.6 PF FP8, 14 PF FP4 and 4.4 TB/s; a 980 in 2029. Slide 25.")
add("7","register2025deepseekascend","The Register",2025,"DeepSeek's R2 training on Huawei Ascend reportedly failed (August 14, 2025)",None,"https://www.theregister.com/2025/08/14/dodgy_huawei_deepseek/","Press, secondary source (relaying the Financial Times). DeepSeek never completed a successful R2 training run on Ascend, citing unstable chips, slow interconnect and immature software, and went back to H20s for training. Slide 25.")
add("7","recode2025chinachips","Recode China AI",2025,"Who will fill Nvidia's AI chip void in China?",None,"https://recodechinaai.substack.com/p/who-will-fill-nvidias-ai-chip-void","Analyst newsletter, secondary source. Hanguang 800 (12 nm, 17 billion transistors, 820 TOPS), Kunlun 2 (7 nm, 128 TFLOP/s FP16, about 120 W), Cambricon MLU370 (96 TF) and MLU590 (345 TF, FP8). Slide 27.")
add("7","caixin2025kunlun","Caixin Global",2025,"Baidu unveils ambitious AI chip roadmap targeting 1 million-card cluster by 2030 (November 14, 2025)",None,"https://www.caixinglobal.com/2025-11-14/baidu-unveils-ambitious-ai-chip-roadmap-targeting-1-million-card-cluster-by-2030-102382580.html","Press, secondary source. Kunlun M100 (2026, inference) and M300 (2027, training), the 30,000-card P800 cluster of April 2025, 512-card nodes in 2026, a million cards by 2030. Slide 27.")
add("7","trendforce2025thead","TrendForce",2025,"Alibaba T-Head PPU lands China Unicom deal, reportedly matches Nvidia H20 performance (September 17, 2025)",None,"https://www.trendforce.com/news/2025/09/17/news-alibaba-t-head-ppu-lands-china-unicom-deal-reportedly-matches-nvidia-h20-performance/","Analyst press, secondary source. The PPU: 96 GB HBM2e, 700 GB/s chip to chip, domestic 7 nm; a 16,384-card China Unicom order. Slide 27.")
add("7","trendforce2026cambricon","TrendForce",2026,"China GPU race intensifies: Cambricon turns profitable in 2025, Moore Threads and MetaX narrow losses (March 9, 2026)",None,"https://www.trendforce.com/news/2026/03/09/news-china-gpu-race-intensifies-cambricon-turns-profitable-in-2025-moore-threads-metax-narrow-losses/","Analyst press, secondary source. Cambricon's 2025 revenue of RMB 6.5B (up 453 percent) and net profit of RMB 2.06B after a 2024 loss; Moore Threads and MetaX revenue. Slide 27.")
add("7","nvidia2025h20","NVIDIA (SEC Form 8-K)",2025,"Form 8-K: H20 export license requirement (April 9, 2025, signed April 15)",None,"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1045810/000104581025000082/nvda-20250409.htm","Filing (SEC). The license requirement for the H20 notified April 9, made indefinite April 14, with up to about $5.5B of charges; the April 2025 step on the policy timeline. Slide 27.")
add("7","mofo2025diffusion","Morrison Foerster",2025,"BIS issues interim final rule: framework for artificial intelligence diffusion (February 4, 2025)",None,"https://www.mofo.com/resources/insights/250204-bis-issues-interim-final-rule","Law-firm summary, secondary source. The January 13, 2025 rule and its three country tiers (authorized, restricted including China, all others), with the May 2025 rescission noted. Slide 27.")
add("7","kirkland2025rescission","Kirkland and Ellis",2025,"BIS rescission of the Biden administration's AI diffusion rule (May 27, 2025)",None,"https://www.kirkland.com/publications/kirkland-alert/2025/05/bis-rescission-of-the-biden-administration","Law-firm summary, secondary source. The May 13, 2025 rescission and the GP10 guidance naming Ascend 910B, 910C and 910D as presumptively made in violation of US controls. Slide 27.")
add("7","ajc2025fifteenpercent","Associated Press (via The Atlanta Journal-Constitution)",2025,"Nvidia, AMD to pay 15% of China chip sale revenue to US government (August 2025)",None,"https://www.ajc.com/news/2025/08/nvidia-amd-to-pay-15-of-china-chip-sale-revenue-to-us-government-2","Press, secondary source. H20 and MI308 sales resumed with 15 percent of China revenue to the US government as a license condition (FT, confirmed to AP by an official). Slide 27.")
add("7","bloomberg2025rtxpro","Bloomberg",2025,"China agency orders firms to stop buying Nvidia AI chip, FT says (September 17, 2025)",None,"https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2025-09-17/china-agency-orders-firms-to-stop-buying-nvidia-ai-chip-ft-says","Press, secondary source. The Cyberspace Administration of China told Alibaba and ByteDance to stop testing and cancel orders for the RTX Pro 6000D; the last point on the policy timeline. Slide 27.")

# ---------------- 8 Emerging designs (slides 28-30)
add("8","siliconangle2025dmatrix","SiliconANGLE",2025,"Chip startup d-Matrix raises $275M to speed up inference with memory-compute (November 12, 2025)",None,"https://siliconangle.com/2025/11/12/chip-startup-d-matrix-raises-275m-speed-inference-memory-compute/","Press, secondary source. The $275M round at $2B; Corsair with 2 GB of SRAM per card, part of it repurposed as multipliers, 256 GB LPDDR5 behind, '9,600 TOPS' in MXINT4 (vendor); Raptor (2026) to stack DRAM on 4 nm (vendor plan). For the chiplet count (two chips of four 6 nm chiplets per card) use the ServeTheHome Hot Chips 2025 entry. Slides 3 and 28.")
add("8","sth2025dmatrixhc","ServeTheHome",2025,"d-Matrix presents Corsair, an in-memory computing architecture for inference, at Hot Chips 2025",None,"https://www.servethehome.com/d-matrix-presents-corsair-an-in-memory-computing-architecture-for-inference-at-hot-chips-2025/","Press, secondary source. The Hot Chips 2025 talk: a Corsair card is two chips of four chiplets each, eight TSMC 6 nm chiplets with 2 GB of SRAM in all, 256 GB of LPDDR5X, 275 to 550 W; the Pavehawk 3D-DRAM test vehicle. Slide 28.")
add("8","gomezluna2021upmem","Gomez-Luna, El Hajj, Fernandez, Giannoula, Oliveira and Mutlu",2021,"Benchmarking a new paradigm: an experimental analysis of a real processing-in-memory architecture","2105.03814",None,"Primary paper. The first independent characterization of commercial processing-in-DRAM (UPMEM DIMMs with 128 DRAM processing units each): where moving compute to the memory pays and where it does not. Slide 28.")
add("8","techcrunch2023mythic","TechCrunch",2023,"AI chip startup Mythic rises from the ashes with $13M, new CEO (March 9, 2023)",None,"https://techcrunch.com/2023/03/09/ai-chip-startup-mythic-rises-from-the-ashes-with-13m-new-ceo","Press, secondary source. The analog flash-in-memory company nearly out of money in November 2022, revived with $13M and a defense focus (before the $125M round of December 2025, separate entry). Slides 28 and 35.")
add("8","businesswire2025mythic","Mythic (BusinessWire)",2025,"Mythic raises $125 million (December 17, 2025)",None,"https://www.businesswire.com/news/home/20251217546249/en/","Vendor press release. An oversubscribed $125M round three years after the near-shutdown of November 2022; the analog in-memory company back in business for edge inference. Slides 28 and 35.")
add("8","hpcwire2025untether","HPCwire",2025,"Untether AI team acquired by AMD; product support discontinued (June 5, 2025)",None,"https://www.hpcwire.com/off-the-wire/untether-ai-team-acquired-by-amd-product-support-discontinued/","Press release, secondary source. Untether ends supply and support of speedAI and its SDK as AMD takes the team. Slides 28, 29 and 35.")
add("8","cnx2026taalas","CNX Software",2026,"Taalas HC1 hardwired Llama 3.1 8B AI accelerator delivers up to 17,000 tokens/s (February 22, 2026)",None,"https://www.cnx-software.com/2026/02/22/taalas-hc1-hardwired-llama-3-1-8b-ai-accelerator-delivers-up-to-17000-tokens-s/","Press, secondary source. HC1: Llama 3.1 8B in the metal layers, TSMC 6 nm, 815 mm2, 53 billion transistors, mixed 3- and 6-bit parameters, close to 17,000 tokens/s for one user. Slide 29.")
add("8","nyu2026amdtaalas","NYU Shanghai RITS",2026,"AMD acquires Taalas, the startup etching LLMs into silicon (August 2026)",None,"https://rits.shanghai.nyu.edu/ai/amd-acquires-taalas-the-startup-etching-llms-into-silicon/","Secondary source. AMD's definitive agreement of August 6, 2026 to buy Taalas, terms undisclosed, closing expected in Q4 2026. Slides 29 and 34.")
add("8","gadgetscout2026etched","GadgetScout",2026,"Etched reaches $10.3bn valuation with SK Hynix backing (August 2, 2026)",None,"https://www.gadgetscout.co.uk/articles/etched-reaches-10-3bn-valuation-with-sk-hynix-backing.html","Press, secondary source. A $300M Series C at $10.3B (July 23, 2026), followed in August by $700M at $21B (separate entry); Sohu on TSMC N4P with 144 GB, A0 silicon in June 2026, no independent benchmark; the 500,000 tokens/s claim for an eight-chip server, which is aggregate throughput, not one user's speed. Slide 29.")
add("8","aiweekly2026etched","AI Weekly",2026,"Etched doubles to $21B in $700M round led by Jane Street (August 18, 2026)",None,"https://aiweekly.co/alerts/etched-doubles-to-21b-in-700m-round-led-by-jane-street","Press, secondary source. $700M at $21B three weeks after the $300M round at $10.3B, so $1B in July and August 2026 with still no independent benchmark of Sohu; the money-before-silicon row on slide 29. Slides 29 and 34.")
add("8","implicator2026positron","Implicator",2026,"Positron raises $875 million at $5 billion before its Asimov chip tapes out (September 10, 2026)",None,"https://www.implicator.ai/positron-raises-875-million-at-5-billion-before-its-asimov-chip-tapes-out.md","Press, secondary source. Atlas on Agilex 7 FPGAs with HBM and DDR5 (50+ racks at Oracle); Asimov on N3P with 288 GB to 2.3 TB of LPDDR5X, tape-out end 2026, volume H2 2027, figures from simulation. Slide 29.")
add("8","marvell2025celestial","Marvell Technology (SEC Form 8-K, Ex. 99.1)",2025,"Marvell to acquire Celestial AI (December 2, 2025)",None,"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1835632/000119312525305289/d34367dex991.htm","Filing (SEC). $1.0B cash and $2.25B in stock up front, up to $2.25B more on revenue milestones; the Photonic Fabric chiplet at 16 Tb/s, 3D co-packaged with XPUs. Slides 29 and 30.")
add("8","lightmatter2026llms","Lightmatter",2026,"Lightmatter product summary (llms.txt)",None,"https://lightmatter.co/llms.txt","Vendor page. Passage M1000 (114 Tb/s on a 4,000 mm2 photonic interposer) and the L200 co-packaged optics; Envise placed in a 2030-plus full photonic stack, not cancelled. For L200 rates use the DCD entry: 32 to 34 Tb/s for the L200 and 64 Tb/s for the L200X per chip, more than 200 Tb/s only per multi-chip package. Slide 30.")
add("8","dcd2025lightmatter","DatacenterDynamics",2025,"Lightmatter unveils M1000 and L200 Passage photonic interconnects",None,"https://datacenterdynamics.com/en/news/lightmatter-unveils-m1000-and-l200-passage-photonic-interconnects","Press, secondary source. The M1000 interposer at 114 Tb/s over 256 fibers; the L200 co-packaged optical engine at 32 to 34 Tb/s and the L200X at 64 Tb/s per chip, with more than 200 Tb/s claimed only per multi-chip XPU package. Slide 30.")
add("8","techpowerup2024halapoint","TechPowerUp",2024,"Intel builds world's largest neuromorphic system to enable more sustainable AI (April 17, 2024)",None,"https://Techpowerup.com/321645/intel-builds-worlds-largest-neuromorphic-system-to-enable-more-sustainable-ai","Vendor release (republished). Hala Point at Sandia: 1,152 Loihi 2 chips, up to 1.15 billion neurons, up to 20 petaops, 2,600 W maximum. Slide 30.")
add("8","gonzalez2024spinnaker2","Gonzalez, Huang, Kelber, Nazeer et al. (TU Dresden)",2024,"SpiNNaker2: a large-scale neuromorphic system for event-based and asynchronous machine learning","2401.04491",None,"Primary paper. 152 Arm cores per chip with local SRAM, 48-chip boards, a multi-million-core machine: the MIMD counterpoint to Loihi 2 among neuromorphic research systems. Slide 30.")
add("8","modha2023northpole","Modha (IBM)",2023,"NorthPole: neural inference at the frontier of energy, space, and time (October 19, 2023; companion to Modha et al., Science 382(6668))",None,"https://modha.org/2023/10/northpole-neural-inference-at-the-frontier-of-energy-space-and-time","Author's page for the Science paper, with a free full-text link. 12 nm, 22 billion transistors, 800 mm2, 256 cores, 224 MB on chip and no off-chip memory; the near-memory limit case. Slides 28 and 30.")
add("8","modha2024northpolellm","Modha (IBM)",2024,"Breakthrough low-latency, high-energy-efficiency LLM inference performance using NorthPole (September 26, 2024, IEEE HPEC)",None,"https://modha.org/2024/09/breakthrough-low-latency-high-energy-efficiency-llm-inference-performance-using-northpole","Author's summary of an HPEC 2024 paper. A 3B model on 16 NorthPole cards in 2U at 28,356 tokens/s, under 1 ms per token per user, 72.7 times the energy efficiency of 'the next lowest-latency GPU' (IBM's measurement; IBM's blog does not name the GPU, which slide 30 reads as an H100). Slide 30.")
add("8","debole2025northpole","DeBole, Appuswamy, McGlohon et al. (IBM)",2025,"A scalable NorthPole system with end-to-end vertical integration for low-latency and energy-efficient LLM inference","2511.15950",None,"Primary paper. 288 NorthPole cards in 18 2U servers: 115 peta-ops at INT4, 3.7 PB/s, 30 kW in one rack, serving 8B models to 28 users at 2.8 ms per token or a 70B model; the step from prototype to rack. Slide 30.")

# ---------------- 9 Measured (slides 31-34)
add("9","peng2023ipurdu","Peng, Choudhury, Ding, Barker, Geng and Li (UConn, PNNL, Rochester)",2023,"Evaluating emerging AI/ML accelerators: IPU, RDU, and NVIDIA/AMD GPUs","2311.04417",None,"Independent evaluation paper. A side-by-side specification table (SN10: 40 billion transistors, 640 PCUs and PMUs, 320 MB SRAM, 325 TFLOP/s, 1.5 TB DRAM) and measured kernels on the IPU, the RDU and GPUs. Slides 17 and 31.")
add("9","emani2023llm","Emani, Foreman, Sastry, Xie et al. (Argonne)",2023,"A comprehensive performance study of large language models on novel AI accelerators","2310.04607",None,"Independent evaluation paper. GPT-2 XL, GenSLM and sparse GPT-3 runs on A100, SN30, CS-2, Bow Pod64, Gaudi2 and MI250 at the ALCF; the closest thing to a neutral LLM benchmark for the dataflow machines, which skipped MLPerf. Slides 32 and 35.")
add("9","mattson2020mlperf","Mattson et al.",2020,"MLPerf Training benchmark (MLSys 2020)","1910.01500",None,"Primary paper. The time-to-train method, the reference models and the closed and open divisions behind every Training round on the participation chart. Slide 32.")
add("9","mlcommons_training_results","MLCommons",2022,"MLPerf Training results repositories (training_results_v0.5 to v6.0; this link is v2.1, November 2022)",None,"https://github.com/mlcommons/training_results_v2.1","Benchmark consortium, open data. One GitHub repository per round, with a directory per submitter and systems/*.json per system; the primary record for the Training dots on slide 32. v2.1 is the round with neither Google nor any IPU entry; change the version in the URL for other rounds. Slides 12, 18 and 32.")
add("9","mlcommons_inference_results","MLCommons",2024,"MLPerf Inference results repositories (inference_results_v0.5 to v6.0; this link is v4.0, March 2024)",None,"https://github.com/mlcommons/inference_results_v4.0","Benchmark consortium, open data. The primary record for the Inference circles on slide 32: TPU entries only in v0.5, v3.1, v4.0 and v5.0 (Google's v4.1, v5.1 and v6.0 entries are NVIDIA systems); v4.0 is Qualcomm's last round and has TPU v5e and Gaudi 2. Slides 24 and 32.")
add("9","mlcommons2025training50","MLCommons",2025,"MLPerf Training v5.0 results (June 4, 2025)",None,"https://mlcommons.org/2025/06/mlperf-training-v5-0-results","Benchmark consortium, open. Twenty submitters with AMD new; TPU Trillium the one non-GPU processor among the twelve; Google's last Training round before it skipped 5.1. Slide 32.")
add("9","mlcommons2026training60","MLCommons",2026,"Supplemental results discussion for MLPerf Training v6.0 (June 2026)",None,"https://mlcommons.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/MLPerf-Training-v6.0-Supplemental-Discussion-UNDER-EMBARGO-UNTIL-6_16_26-8_00-AM-PT-1.pdf","Benchmark consortium, open. The submitters' own notes for Training 6.0: Google is listed as a submitter but only AMD and NVIDIA accelerators are named; the basis for 'no TPU result in 6.0'. Slides 12 and 32.")
add("9","aa2026gptoss","Artificial Analysis",2026,"gpt-oss-120B (high): API provider benchmarks (live page, read November 2026)",None,"https://artificialanalysis.ai/models/gpt-oss-120b/providers","Independent benchmark service. Sixteen providers of one model: Cerebras first answer in about 2.1 s at $0.39 per million tokens, the highest price listed; Groq and SambaNova slower to first answer. Read it with a date; it changes. Slide 33.")
add("9","patel2024groq","Patel and Nishball (SemiAnalysis)",2024,"Groq inference tokenomics: speed, but at what cost? (February 21, 2024)",None,"https://newsletter.semianalysis.com/p/groq-inference-tokenomics-speed-but","Analyst note, secondary source. 576 chips (8 racks of 9 servers of 8) to serve Mixtral, 230 MB SRAM and about 725 mm2 on GlobalFoundries 14 nm per chip, against an H100 with about $1,150 of HBM; the cost-per-token argument. Slides 8, 16 and 33.")
